ot/issues/comments/4569395862","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119465#issuecomment-4569395862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119465","id":4569395862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEFtylg","user":{"login":"Cautami","id":219921783,"node_id":"U_kgDODRu9dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219921783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami","html_url":"https://github.com/Cautami","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T00:25:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T00:26:42Z","body":"I have this issue too on Plasma 6.6.5 with Wayland + Godot Wayland\nAs the SC2 is the only controller I have this is particularly annoying, but there is a way to work around it. \nIf you use [SISR](https://github.com/Alia5/SISR) you can emulate a proper xbox360 controller which Godot will actually be capable of reading, you won't have all the fancy features, but for generic controller testing (my use case) this works pretty well until a fix is found. \nIt should be noted that the issue includes the editor, attempting to rebind inputs within the project settings menu with the SC2 won't read input there either.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/45